# Generated output. Every report is reproducible by running the tool, and the
# archive would otherwise add megabytes of HTML to the repo on every run.
reports/
site/
cache/
logs/

# The premarket scan output. The premarket workflow publishes it to the
# market-data branch, where the deployed board polls for it; on main it is just
# generated output like the reports.
premarket/

# sessions/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the recorded 1-minute history
# the practice terminal replays, and Yahoo only serves 7 days back, so it
# cannot be re-fetched once it ages out. Left untracked, the published site
# would fall back to generated candles.

# Your own records. Tracked would mean your trade history and rules ship
# with the code; keep them local and let OneDrive sync them.
journal.json

# Local scratch
_patch.mjs
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
